1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,120
A four-dollar painting

2
00:00:01,120 --> 00:00:04,002
was hiding eight million dollars.

3
00:00:04,002 --> 00:00:06,502
But first, three other weird things

4
00:00:06,502 --> 00:00:08,353
that made people rich.

5
00:00:08,353 --> 00:00:09,433
A stage worker in Dublin

6
00:00:09,433 --> 00:00:12,334
was cleaning up after a Lady Gaga show.

7
00:00:12,334 --> 00:00:12,974
On the floor

8
00:00:12,974 --> 00:00:15,454
he spotted something small and shiny.

9
00:00:15,454 --> 00:00:17,359
He thought it was a guitar pick.

10
00:00:17,359 --> 00:00:19,372
It was one of her fake nails.

11
00:00:19,372 --> 00:00:20,432
He sold it online

12
00:00:20,432 --> 00:00:22,493
for about twelve thousand dollars.

13
00:00:22,493 --> 00:00:23,333
A woman in Miami

14
00:00:23,333 --> 00:00:25,583
did even better with her lunch.

15
00:00:25,583 --> 00:00:28,333
She made a grilled cheese sandwich, took one bite,

16
00:00:28,333 --> 00:00:30,192
and saw a face in the toast.

17
00:00:30,192 --> 00:00:33,172
To her, it looked like the Virgin Mary.

18
00:00:33,172 --> 00:00:34,714
So she kept it.

19
00:00:34,714 --> 00:00:37,084
For ten years.

20
00:00:37,084 --> 00:00:38,804
In 2004, an online casino

21
00:00:38,804 --> 00:00:41,090
paid twenty-eight thousand dollars for it.

22
00:00:41,090 --> 00:00:43,437
Then came a single chicken nugget.

23
00:00:43,437 --> 00:00:46,417
In 2021, someone got a McDonald's nugget

24
00:00:46,417 --> 00:00:49,398
shaped like a crewmate from the game Among Us.

25
00:00:49,398 --> 00:00:50,258
They put it on eBay

26
00:00:50,258 --> 00:00:52,161
for ninety-nine cents.

27
00:00:52,161 --> 00:00:53,841
A hundred and eighty-four bids later,

28
00:00:53,841 --> 00:00:58,771
it sold for ninety-nine thousand, nine hundred and ninety-seven dollars.

29
00:00:58,771 --> 00:01:00,764
Now, the painting.

30
00:01:00,764 --> 00:01:02,964
A man bought it at a flea market in Pennsylvania

31
00:01:02,964 --> 00:01:04,775
for four dollars.

32
00:01:04,775 --> 00:01:07,084
He only wanted the frame.

33
00:01:07,084 --> 00:01:08,054
When he took it apart,

34
00:01:08,054 --> 00:01:11,375
he found a folded paper hidden behind the canvas.

35
00:01:11,375 --> 00:01:14,385
It was an original copy of the Declaration of Independence,

36
00:01:14,385 --> 00:01:17,416
printed in 1776.

37
00:01:17,416 --> 00:01:19,058
Only about two dozen are known.

38
00:01:19,058 --> 00:01:20,188
In 1991

39
00:01:20,188 --> 00:01:23,148
it sold for two point four million dollars.

40
00:01:23,148 --> 00:01:23,888
Nine years later

41
00:01:23,888 --> 00:01:26,530
it sold again, for eight million.

42
00:01:26,530 --> 00:01:28,927
What's the weirdest thing you've ever found?
